+# Tasks
+
+## 1. Atomic redemption persistence
+
+- [x] 1.1 Add `src/repositories/couponRedemptionRepository.ts` with a `redeem()` that, inside one `BEGIN`/`COMMIT`, updates the order's `discount_cents`, `final_amount_cents`, `coupon_code`, inserts one `coupon_redemptions` row and increments `coupons.used_count`, rolling back on any failure. Verify with a repository test in `tests/applyCoupon.test.ts` that all three writes land together and that a failing insert leaves the order, redemption table and used count unchanged.
+
+## 2. Coupon eligibility and discount rules
+
+- [x] 2.1 Extend `src/services/couponService.ts` with `resolveUsable(code, now)` covering existence, `ACTIVE`, `validFrom <= now < validUntil` and the usage limit, throwing `COUPON_NOT_FOUND` / `COUPON_INACTIVE` / `COUPON_NOT_YET_VALID` / `COUPON_EXPIRED` / `COUPON_USAGE_EXHAUSTED`. Verify with unit tests covering each outcome plus `now == validFrom` accepted and `now == validUntil` expired.
+- [x] 2.2 Add `discountFor(coupon, amountCents)` to `CouponService`, computing FIXED value, `floor(amountCents * value / 100)` for PERCENT, honouring `maxDiscountCents` when set, then clamping to `amountCents`. Verify with unit tests for amount 10000 / 20% → 2000, FIXED 1500 → 1500, 999 / 15% → 149, FIXED 3000 on 1000 → 1000, AC-03's 100000 / 20% with no maximum → 20000, and a set maximum capping the result.
+
+## 3. Apply-coupon use case
+
+- [x] 3.1 Add `OrderService.applyCoupon(id, rawCouponCode)` implementing the check order from the spec (body → order exists → `PENDING` → re-applied same code → coupon eligibility → minimum amount), normalising the code, rejecting a repeated identical coupon with `COUPON_ALREADY_APPLIED`, letting a different coupon replace the previous one, and returning the reloaded order. Verify with service tests for each rejection code, the replacement path (AC-08) and `PENDING` status preservation.
+- [x] 3.2 Wire the new repository and service dependency in `src/app.ts` and confirm the existing test suite still passes with `npm test`.
+
+## 4. HTTP endpoint and error contract
+
+- [x] 4.1 Register `POST /orders/:id/apply-coupon` in `src/routes/orders.ts`, passing only the parsed id and the raw `couponCode`. Verify through `app.request(...)` that the response body is byte-identical to the following `GET /orders/:id`, that a blank/non-string/missing `couponCode` returns 400 `INVALID_REQUEST`, and that each of the ten error-table outcomes is produced with its documented status and code.
+- [x] 4.2 Add endpoint tests for `" save20 "` normalising to `SAVE20` (AC-10), for `GET /coupons/:code` showing the incremented `usedCount` plus one new `coupon_redemptions` row after success (AC-09), and for a fixed injected clock resolving `now == validFrom` as success and `now == validUntil` as `COUPON_EXPIRED` (AC-07).
+
+## 5. Integration verification
+
+- [x] 5.1 Run `npm run build`, `npm test` and `openspec validate "apply-coupon-to-order" --strict`; all must pass with the new tests included and no existing test or fixture changed.
+
+## Workflow follow-up
+
+- Archive the change once the review requirements for this project are satisfied.
